    "interpretation": "When a destination GPU cannot copy directly from a resident GPU, the pinned UVM path stages those pages through CPU memory, merges the first-stage tracker into the VA-block tracker, then queues the CPU-to-destination stage against that same tracker. The hybrid bridge reports no cross-provider P2P link, and isolated mode returns NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED if the destination push sees an outstanding entry from another GPU. A completed source tracker is exempt, so the exact failure is conditional on work still being pending at the destination reservation. This is a static control-flow result; it is not a runtime failure, timing measurement, or proof that every migration attempt fails.",
    "migration_behavior": "cross_provider_gpu_staging_can_be_rejected_when_source_tracker_is_pending",
